WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.830
Although most of the Deadpool 2 hype is focused
on Cable, the film will also see the debut

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.480
of another Marvel mutant mercenary: Domino.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.190
A longtime ally of Cable and Deadpool, Domino
has spent the last couple of decades in comics

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:17.050
shooting, stabbing, and punching her way through
any threat — aided by her ability to influence

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.420
probability in her favor.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.300
"I didn't become an X-Man to play it safe.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.980
Besides, we have luck on our side."

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:25.980
"Domino…"

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.679
But there's a lot more to this femme fatale
than a bit of good luck and a full magazine.

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:33.430
Here's the untold truth of Domino.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.000
Fakeout appearance

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.120
Any X-Men fan worth their salt knows that
clones and doppelgängers are practically

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.350
a rite of passage if you're trying to run
with Xavier's crew.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:47.230
Everyone from Jean Grey to Cable has been
subjected to a litany of bizarre, contrived

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.010
sci-fi tropes over the course of their time
with the team.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.100
On a surprising note, Domino actually has
a pretty straightforward history, albeit with

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.490
one exception: Her first appearance in comics.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:02.040
In the grand scheme of things, Domino appears
for the first time in New Mutants #98 alongside

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.040
Deadpool.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.350
If you want to get technical though, Domino's
real debut is X-Force #8.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.670
See, it's revealed that the Domino we meet
in New Mutants #98 is actually the shapeshifter

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.540
mutant Copycat, a.k.a. Vanessa Carlysle.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.950
It isn't until several issues later that the
real Domino reveals herself.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.180
It's appropriate, really.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:23.400
There's nothing more quintessentially X-Men
than a doppelgänger, and Domino covered that

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.550
base immediately upon her debut.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:27.980
Colossal fling

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.800
In the wake of the crossover story Avengers
vs. X-Men, Domino finds herself joining Cable's

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.659
newest spinoff team, X-Force.

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:38.360
The team members are now fugitives on the
run from the Avengers, and many characters

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.970
are trying to cope with the fallout of the
cataclysmic war in Avengers vs. X-Men.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.450
Colossus in particular finds himself grieving
the loss of his relationship with Kitty Pryde.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.160
Enter Domino, who quickly hits it off with
the big guy.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.410
The new relationship doesn't last long, leaving
the fling as little more than a strange, brief

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:56.530
footnote in both of their lives.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.530
Original Six Pack

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:02.580
Colossus aside, most comics readers are more
used to seeing Domino work with the time-traveling

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.630
mutant Cable.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:08.470
The two have a long history together as best
friends, teammates, and sometime love interests.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:12.620
Cable and Domino first met as members of the
mercenary team Six Pack, formerly known as

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:13.769
Wild Pack.

00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:18.040
Even after the Six Pack disbanded, Cable and
Domino found themselves sticking together.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.930
Eventually, Cable joined the New Mutants team
— which later became X-Force — and got

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.319
Domino her gig with the group.

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:25.969
Birthday gift

00:02:25.969 --> 00:02:29.680
One of Domino's more interesting relationships
is with Wolverine.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.099
Sometimes it's a friendship, sometimes a rivalry,
and other times it's even been a full-fledged

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:35.099
relationship.

00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:38.129
One of the highlights of their time together
was when Domino bought Wolverine a car for

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:39.129
his birthday.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:42.139
It happens in the comic mini-series X-Force:
Sex and Violence.

00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:47.389
The story wraps up with Wolverine realizing
that Domino secretly kept $37 million that

00:02:47.389 --> 00:02:48.650
was supposed to go to charity.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:53.310
Right as he's about to get mad, she rolls
up outside with a pristine classic Mustang

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.480
and wishes him a happy birthday.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.480
It's a little sleazy and a little sweet — the
perfect combination for Domino and Wolverine.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:04.060
As they drive off, Wolverine realizes Domino
has stashed their nemesis Razorfist in the

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.060
trunk.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:08.269
We guess she can only do so many nice things
in a single day.

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:10.010
Domino vs. Punisher

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:13.829
There are few people in the Marvel universe
more terrifying than Frank Castle.

00:03:13.829 --> 00:03:17.620
It's telling that the guy doesn't have a single
superpower and still hasn't been taken down

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.680
by a single superhero who's tried to end his
vigilante days.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.569
Still, it hasn't stopped people from trying,
and one of those people is Domino.

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:28.870
In Punisher War Journal, Domino goes after
Castle because he's been accused of massacring

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:29.870
civilians.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:34.000
Tasked with taking him down by an old acquaintance,
Domino is the only person on the team who

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.440
maintains that Castle is probably innocent.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:40.189
She turns out to be right, and the climax
sees the Punisher duking it out with the real

00:03:40.189 --> 00:03:42.389
criminal behind the crime: Jigsaw.

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:45.449
Justice is served — which is great and all
— but we don't get to find out who would

00:03:45.449 --> 00:03:48.889
win between these two warriors in a head-to-head
brawl.

00:03:48.889 --> 00:03:50.319
Family reunion

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:55.480
In the 2003 mini-series Domino, we find out
that Domino gained her skills as a mercenary

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.489
through Project Armageddon, a program designed
to create the "Perfect Weapon."

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:03.480
She was considered a failure, and her mother
went on to break her out of the project.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.040
After that, her mother disappeared.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.400
Years into her career as a mercenary, Domino
meets a boy named Lazarus who has the same

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.519
distinctive eye marking as she does.

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:16.630
Lazarus is revealed to be Domino's half-brother,
and as it turns out, he's the Perfect Weapon.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:19.659
Unfortunately, their mom isn't quite so keen
on her kids hanging out.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:24.199
With a crew of violent religious zealots,
she sets out to put an end to both of them.

00:04:24.199 --> 00:04:28.690
Domino is forced to shoot her mom to protect
Lazarus, making this the worst family reunion

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.400
in history.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.770
Stryfe surprise

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:36.639
Perhaps no other X-Men character better embodies
the spirit and aesthetic of the '90s than

00:04:36.639 --> 00:04:37.639
Stryfe.

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:41.330
He's a clone of Cable from the future whose
suit is made of giant knives, more or less.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:46.379
Being an X-Men character, there are plenty
of alternate-universe versions of Stryfe,

00:04:46.379 --> 00:04:48.680
and
in X-Force, vol. 2 #4, Domino actually takes

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.479
on the identity of one of them.

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:54.580
This version of Domino comes to the primary
Marvel universe from an alternate future and

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:59.539
joins a new incarnation of the Mutant Liberation
Front founded by Cable and former X-Force

00:04:59.539 --> 00:05:00.550
teammate Shatterstar.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.940
Of all the alternate Dominos, this is one
of the coolest.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:08.319
Not only does the skilled mercenary make great
use of Stryfe's armor, but longtime readers

00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:12.289
loved seeing Domino embody her best friend's
arch nemesis and evil clone.

00:05:12.289 --> 00:05:13.389
Thanks for watching!

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:16.430
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.660
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
